<title>USA: Dry conditions seen for parts of U.S. Midwest corn.</title>
<headline>Dry conditions seen for parts of U.S. Midwest corn.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-07-14</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hot, dry conditions are expected to continue for at least five days in pockets of Illinois, Iowa and Missouri, which may stress the corn crop during its pollination period, meteorologists said.</p>
<p>&quot;For the next five days, we will see dry conditions in the the dry areas of western Illinois and extreme southeastern Iowa,&quot; said Kevin Marcus, agricultural meteorologist and director of CROPCAST Services Marketing in Rockville, Md.</p>
<p>&quot;The focus is in western Illinois,&quot; he said, noting the corn corp in that area may have a tough pollination period because of dry topsoils and a forecast for hot temperatures.</p>
</text>
